KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
other.c --validate-goto-model
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ wrap: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
Invariant check failed
--
A C unit linked after a C++ unit declares a typedef of a struct the C++
unit also declares; the two struct types differ (C++ qualifies member
names), so the linker renames the C typedef.  It was renamed to a string
built from its type, while the C types written with the typedef still
named the old symbol: --validate-goto-model stopped with "locale_pointers
not found".  Typedefs are now renamed with a $link suffix, as other
symbols are, and so are the typedef names that types record.  The
Universal CRT's _locale_t and stdio.h's inline functions hit this when
the C library models are linked (VS 2026 CI).
